# C# / .NET 8 Coding Standards

## Project Overview

- **Framework**: ASP.NET Core 8 (Web API)
- **ORM**: Entity Framework Core 8 + Dapper
- **Database**: SQL Server via `Microsoft.Data.SqlClient`
- **Style**: your coding style guide (see `.editorconfig`)

## Naming Conventions

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Interface | `I` + PascalCase | `IUserRepository` |
| Class / Struct | PascalCase | `UserService`, `WeatherForecast` |
| Method | PascalCase | `GetUserById`, `CreateOrder` |
| Property | PascalCase | `FirstName`, `IsActive` |
| Private field | `_camelCase` | `_logger`, `_dbConnection` |
| Parameter | camelCase | `userId`, `pageNumber` |
| Constant | PascalCase | `MaxRetryCount`, `DefaultPageSize` |
| File name | PascalCase (match class) | `UserService.cs`, `CreateUserDto.cs` |

## Code Layout

### Braces — Allman style

```csharp
// ✅ Opening brace on new line
public async Task<IActionResult> GetUser(string id)
{
    var user = await _context.Users.FindAsync(id);
    if (user == null)
    {
        return NotFound();
    }
    return Ok(user);
}

// ❌ K&R style (not used in this project)
public async Task<IActionResult> GetUser(string id) {
    var user = await _context.Users.FindAsync(id);
    if (user == null) {
        return NotFound();
    }
    return Ok(user);
}
```

### Line Length

- Max **120 characters** per line
- Break long method chains, LINQ queries, and parameter lists

### File Structure

```csharp
// 1. Using statements (sorted alphabetically, .NET 8 implicit usings optional)
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;

// 2. Namespace
namespace LAP_API.Controllers;

// 3. Class declaration
public class UserController : ControllerBase
{
    // 4. Private fields (_camelCase)
    private readonly ILogger<UserController> _logger;
    private readonly ApplicationDbContext _context;

    // 5. Constructor
    public UserController(
        ILogger<UserController> logger,
        ApplicationDbContext context)
    {
        _logger = logger;
        _context = context;
    }

    // 6. Public methods
    // 7. Private methods
}
```

## Controller Conventions

- All controllers inherit from `ControllerBase`
- Use `[ApiController]` attribute on every controller
- Route: `[Route("api/[controller]")]` or `[Route("api/[controller]/[action]")]`
- Action methods return `IActionResult` or `ActionResult<T>`
- Use `GetCurrentUserId()` from base class if available, otherwise inject `IUserIdAccessor`
- Every mutating endpoint (POST/PUT/DELETE) requires `[Authorize]` or explicit `[AllowAnonymous]`

## API Response Patterns

```csharp
// ✅ Standard success
return Ok(result);
return CreatedAtAction(nameof(GetUser), new { id = user.Id }, user);

// ✅ Standard error — never expose exception details
return BadRequest(new { message = "Validation failed." });
return NotFound(new { message = "User not found." });
return StatusCode(500, new { message = "An error occurred. Please try again." });

// ❌ Never do this — leaks internal details
return BadRequest(ex.Message);
```

## Data Access

### EF Core — Safe Queries

```csharp
// ✅ Safe — parameterized automatically
var user = await _context.Users.FirstOrDefaultAsync(u => u.Id == id);

// ✅ Safe — parameterized raw query
await _context.Database.ExecuteSqlRawAsync(
    "UPDATE Users SET Name = {0} WHERE Id = {1}", name, id);

// ❌ Never — string interpolation in SQL
await _context.Database.ExecuteSqlRawAsync(
    $"UPDATE Users SET Name = '{name}' WHERE Id = '{id}'");
```

### Dapper — Safe Queries

```csharp
// ✅ Parameterized
var user = await _connection.QueryFirstOrDefaultAsync<User>(
    "SELECT * FROM Users WHERE Id = @Id",
    new { Id = id });

// ❌ Never
_connection.Query("SELECT * FROM Users WHERE Id = '" + id + "'");
```

## Async/Await

- All I/O-bound operations must be `async`/`await`
- Never use `.Result` or `.Wait()` — use `await`
- Controller actions returning `Task<IActionResult>`

## Null Handling

- Use nullable reference types (`string?`, `int?`)
- Use null-conditional operator `?.` and null-coalescing `??`
- Prefer pattern matching over `== null`
- Do not suppress nullable warnings without good reason

## LINQ

- Use method syntax for readability; mix with query syntax for complex queries
- Avoid unnecessary `.ToList()` / `.ToArray()` in the middle of chains
- Use `IAsyncEnumerable` for streaming large result sets

## Dependency Injection

```csharp
// Register in Program.cs or extension method
builder.Services.AddScoped<IUserRepository, UserRepository>();

// Inject via constructor
public class UserService
{
    private readonly IUserRepository _userRepository;

    public UserService(IUserRepository userRepository)
    {
        _userRepository = userRepository;
    }
}
```

## Error Handling

```csharp
// Controller-level
try
{
    var result = await _service.DoSomething();
    return Ok(result);
}
catch (UserNotFoundException ex)
{
    _logger.LogWarning(ex, "User not found: {UserId}", ex.UserId);
    return NotFound(new { message = "User not found." });
}
catch (Exception ex)
{
    _logger.LogError(ex, "Unexpected error");
    return StatusCode(500, new { message = "An error occurred. Please try again." });
}
```

## Logging

- Use `ILogger<T>` in every service and controller
- Log at appropriate levels: `LogDebug`, `LogInformation`, `LogWarning`, `LogError`
- Include correlation IDs or user IDs in log context when available
- Never log sensitive data (passwords, tokens, PII)

## Constants & Magic Numbers

```csharp
// ❌ Magic numbers
if (pageSize > 100) { ... }

// ✅ Named constants
private const int MaxPageSize = 100;
if (pageSize > MaxPageSize) { ... }
```

## Attributes

- Use `[Required]`, `[StringLength]`, `[Range]` for validation
- Use `[JsonPropertyName("camelCase")]` for API response naming
- Use `[ProducesResponseType]` on controller actions for Swagger

## Region Directive

- Avoid `#region` / `#endregion` — they hide complexity rather than solve it
- If a file needs regions, split it into multiple files instead

## IDisposable

- Dispose resources properly: `using` statements or DI lifetime management
- Do not call `.Dispose()` manually when DI handles it

## Commenting

- Do not comment obvious code
- Use XML doc comments (`/// <summary>`) on public API surface only
- Explain **why**, not **what**
